abstract: >-
  AL-MIZAN is a complete quantum emulator implemented in pure Python with zero external dependencies,
  unifying state vector simulation (up to 16 qubits), density matrix evolution (up to 8 qubits),
  Steane [[7,1,3]] quantum error correction, zero-noise extrapolation (Richardson), and pedagogical
  GDSII layout generation. It provides sealed SHA-256 mathematical certificates for bounded verifications:
  Point Square Conjecture (PC-1..PC-6 verified by exhaustion on the declared finite domain), Turing theorem on the Riemann strip <= 100
  (29 zeros certified via interval arithmetic), and BSD verification on named elliptic curves.
  A numerical-agreement criterion (EQ-DSI-01..06) decides whether a closed form offered for a measured
  constant is derived or merely coincidental: it reproduces (79 + 48*sqrt(2) + 42*sqrt(3) + 3*sqrt(6))/31104
  to 1.42e-13, scores it at z = 0.5983879635182564 against CODATA 2022, and enumerates all 40,959,999
  forms a + b*sqrt(2) + c*sqrt(3) + d*sqrt(6) with n <= 31104, where the examined form ranks 47th of 82 at
  0.6 sigma and the best coincidence in the retained window is 108 times closer. The verdict is
  bounded to the public text examined and carries no judgment of intent.
  QPU_DISTANT re-reads one already-executed run on a distant quantum processor (job dbpkmr0ou4as73ctrm80
  on ibm_marrakesh, 256 shots on the physical support [0,1], 600 units): it recomputes the outcome
  counters from the provider result table (00 = 126, 01 = 22, 11 = 108, sum 256, so 10 = 0), reports the
  even-parity rate 0.9140625 = 234/256, and confronts it with two derived bounds - the machine median
  bound 0.9258965 is not met (-0.676 sigma) while the real-support bound 0.9114310 is met (+0.150 sigma);
  the 22-vs-0 asymmetry of the two weight-one words rejects the equiprobability null hypothesis at
  p = 4.77e-07 under an exact integer Binom(22, 1/2). The module runs no qubit, tests no AL-MIZAN
  equation and bounds only what a distant execution allows to be written.
  GOULETS bounds the publication bottlenecks measured on this workspace: 23 videos counted, longest 30 s
  against a declared 900 s threshold (870 s of margin), a 99-per-day published quota against a 10-per-day
  ceiling actually observed (ratio 9.9), a measured cadence of 1.3529 per day, 78 files and 1432.543 s in
  stock, 35434115072 free bytes out of 252841029632 (14.01 percent). Four dated, falsifiable bounds - no
  ceiling is claimed to have been lifted.
  SURETE bounds software security instead of promising it: 13 equations and 13 controls. Rice's theorem is
  stated then bounded by the exact enumeration of the 131071 = 2^17 - 1 nonzero words of K = 16; Poisson with a
  common cause is reached by three independent routes (p = 1/5, beta = 1/10 giving s = 1/50 and a = 9/49); the
  patch window is 360-720 h when it is known and 0 h when it is not, so an undisclosed window is only ever
  understated; availability is A = 4380/4381 = 0.999772 at MTBF 8760 h and MTTR 2 h. An obsolescence criterion is
  then applied to six written guarantee statements, with no company and no person named: three fall outside it and
  three hold; the same criterion is turned against this module (C13). 7 OPERATIONAL, 4 SIMULATED, 2 SPECIFIED - no
  proof and no measurement of any real product.
  The same obsolescence criterion also runs as an out-of-registry chain, shipped so that a bare clone replays it:
  solutions_posees_acteurs.py (EQ-SA, 13 equations, 13 controls, 6 OPERATIONAL, 6 SIMULATED, 1 SPECIFIED) judges a
  guarantee statement, never a firm, and records that the video which supplied the theme has neither public chapters
  nor an accessible transcript. It rests on reseau_poids_sparse_mizan.py, a 313000000000000 = 313 * 10^12 addressable
  weight base (EQ-PS-01..09: a BLAKE2b-64 reduced quintuple, only written addresses occupy memory), on
  tokenizer_mizan.py (259 byte-level symbols), on module_tableau_maitre_mizan.py and on the shipped
  TABLEAU_MAITRE_SEQUENTIEL_UNIFIE.csv (454 data rows, 41 strata, 362708 bytes at checkout at v3.5.0). Measured
  in a clone placed outside the author's workspace and re-checked from the ZIP extract: base 9 PASS, 0 FAIL, root
  32d241880c1fc396, exit code 0; EQ-SA 13/13 with and without the CSV on the identical chain digest
  6c39391df55d991b - the CSV weighs on the base, not on the judgment. The registry holds 15 modules, 232 equations
  and 232 controls, and the manifest 285 entries carrying no date.
  v3.6.0 changes no registry module. It refreshes the shipped master table: the EQ-SB strate S41 takes the file from
  454 to 470 data rows and from 41 to 42 strata, i.e. 389164 bytes and SHA-256 d3ad50d52d9cb081... at checkout,
  388693 and 293b8f7cf17b43e7... in the blob (OID 5c90894e5cc04e17), the gap being the 471 line endings that
  eol=crlf restores; the same CSV leaves the base root unchanged at 32d241880c1fc396. It adds to
  docs/API_PASSERELLE_VPS.md the eight route rows of the two registers this deposit ships (EQ-SA and EQ-SB), copied
  verbatim from the workshop table, together with a dated statement of its own incompleteness: of the 135 keys of
  the production gateway dictionary PAGES_PUBLIQUES, 86 - 51 families - still have no row here, because those pages
  live on the workshop side and are not shipped; the check is replayable offline (read the keys, search each /route
  in the file, count the absences), and what is claimed is that the listed routes are served, not that the list is
  exhaustive. It also records the recipe behind the EQ-SA chain digest, until then left out, which is why a replay
  could return another value: SHA-256 over UTF-8 of the 13 'EQ-nn|result' records followed by the 13
  'Cnn|expected|obtained|ok' records, each record separated from the next by a single newline, first 16 hexadecimal
  digits; the variant without the separator gives bd397aa7a35bb616. Replayed on 2026-11-14 inside this deposit:
  base 9 PASS, 0 FAIL, root 32d241880c1fc396, exit code 0; EQ-SA 13/13 on digest 6c39391df55d991b;
  FONDATION/OUTILS/audit_piliers.py --tous on 15 modules, 232 equations, 232 controls, exit code 0.
  v3.7.0 ships the EQ-TLU register as a root-level module: accomplissement_313t_mizan.py, 9 equations and 9 controls, separating the
  three senses of 'accomplishing the 313T weights' - volume REFUSED (626 TB dense in bf16, 2504 TB in float64, against the free space
  measured on the machine, margin recomputed at every run by C06), structure ACCOMPLISHED (the radices close exactly on 313T, a
  bijection in both directions, a partition into 313 fibres), function ACCOMPLISHED (one weight per address, computable in O(1) with no
  storage) - plus a grid of 313000 anchors actually written, 1e-9 of the capacity, its Merkle root recomputed twice to the same value.
  C07 bounds the enumeration with two timed throughput measures at two different sizes; the extrapolated time counts in centuries and
  was never run. No proof, no machine under power. Copy fidelity is measured, not asserted: workshop file 54346 bytes
  (2337507942a7f444...), this copy 54676 (4b4354fab6bbb513...), the diff being one hunk of four docstring lines, with identical syntax
  trees once the docstrings are removed; the test copy renders 43 tests against the workshop's 44 collected, the dropped method being
  the site-manifest membership test, which reads three files this deposit does not ship - and whose local equivalent cannot be green at
  the moment that matters, since the seal is taken on the blobs of the content commit. Replayed inside this deposit: 9 PASS, 0 FAIL,
  verdicts root af29ebe38dd79b3b..., the exact digest carried by the three published pages, and 9 attacks captured out of 9. One first
  run went red here (Ran 43 tests in 121.721s, failures=2, compte 8 PASS / 1 FAIL and 8 of 9 mutations captured); every replay since is
  green, including this one (Ran 43 tests, OK, 74 s). The cause is not established - the runner was not instrumented at that moment -
  but the candidate set is closed by experiment: only two controls read outside the module, and forcing _mesurer_ram() to return
  'unavailable', which is what GlobalMemoryStatusEx yields when it fails, reproduces that exact pair of symptoms on EQ-TLU-06, as does
  forcing rapport_debits outside the band, at 0.4 and at 2.6, on EQ-TLU-07. 2000 consecutive calls to _mesurer_ram() never returned
  'unavailable' (0.13 s, machine at 87 percent RAM load, 1.02 GB free), while six rapport_debits measures under four worker threads
  spread from 0.7885 to 1.6191 inside a band that stops at 0.5 and 2.0: throughput is the tighter of the two instruments. Neither band
  nor threshold was loosened to buy a colour. The embedded master table moves from 470 to 482 data rows and from 42 to 43 strata, strate
  S42 carrying the twelve EQ-TLU rows: 411573 bytes and SHA-256 189c8c9b5a88cd1a... at Windows checkout, 411090 and cf47914b42ba6da1...
  in the LF blob (OID f96606dde09c54f2), the gap being exactly the 483 line endings that eol=crlf restores. Replayed on this CSV:
  reseau_poids_sparse_mizan.py --controler holds 9 PASS, 0 FAIL, root 32d241880c1fc396, exit code 0 - the base verdicts root does not
  depend on the row count - and solutions_posees_acteurs.py holds 13/13 on the unchanged chain digest 6c39391df55d991b. The
  materialisation counter does follow the table: the same line prints 185202 weights here against 175509 on the 470-row file, because
  materialiser_registre writes rows in file order and draws no randomness. The EQ-TLU module displays the base's published constant
  (materialises_socle_publie = 175509, line 512) and C05 confronts that constant with the 200000 ceiling; both values pass under it. The
  drift is recorded here and in docs/API_PASSERELLE_VPS.md instead of being smoothed, and the three published pages and the served JSON
  still carry 175509. The four suites under tests/ render 53 + 25 + 31 + 43 = 152 tests, each OK with exit code 0; with the 10 tests of
  horloge_noyau the out-of-registry count is 162 and the composed total 774, of which only the 162 was replayed at this hour.
  docs/API_PASSERELLE_VPS.md gains four route rows copied byte for byte from the workshop table, taking it from 104 to 108 rows; under
  the recipe that file states itself, absences go from 91 in 53 families to 86 in 51 families over the 145 current keys of
  PAGES_PUBLIQUES, the five recovered keys being exactly those of EQ-TLU. The audit registry is untouched: 15 modules CONFORME,
  232 equations, 232 controls, exit code 0.
  Strict honesty constraints: every artifact carries its computational bound, no open millennium problem
  is claimed as solved. Developed by M. Ahmed EL BAHLOUL under the IMAM8MAHDI initiative.
